<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - Basis steady to lower.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - Basis steady to lower.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean meal basis offers in U.S. cash markets were steady to lower Monday amid pessimism about export prospects and growing supplies, several cash brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The export market is backing off and the soybean basis is weakening,&quot; a Tennessee broker said. &quot;If the crush is going to stay around 30 (million bushels), there's going to be a lot of meal out there.&quot;</p>
<p>U.S. Gulf CIF and FOB values were higher in thin trading as shippers bid higher to meet prompt deadlines, an Ohio River broker said.</p>
<p>Elsewhere, movement was slow as end-users waited for the CBOT December contract to expire. That contract was trading at a $10 per ton premium to the January.  </p>
